WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.500
Придет.

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:02.000
Это means hello in Russian.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:07.300
Welcome to Privet Rusky, episode 34, for the 4th of June, 2026.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:11.540
I'm Olya, and today we are going to learn some really fun Russian words.

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:12.260
Ready?

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:13.100
Поехали.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:14.280
That means let's go.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:16.240
Our word of the day is kit.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:17.300
Listen closely.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:17.760
Kit.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:19.400
Now say it slowly with me.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:19.880
Kit.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:21.620
This word means whale.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.240
Picture a huge friendly submarine that sings songs underwater.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.360
That picture will help you remember kit every time.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.040
Now try it in a sentence.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.200
Большой кид плавает в море.

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.120
Say the whole sentence after me.

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:36.240
Большой кид плавает в море.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.260
One more time at normal speed.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:40.440
Большой кид плавает в море.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:41.300
Great job.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.380
Let's add more animal words that go with our theme.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:46.100
Start with животное.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:47.160
Животное.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:48.640
This means animal.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:49.680
Repeat after me.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:50.600
Животное.

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:54.360
Notice how it sounds a little like G-water-cute animal.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.880
That sound link makes it easy to recall.

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.940
Next comes обезьяна.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:00:59.860
Обезьяна.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.040
This means monkey.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:02.120
Say it with me.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:03.140
Обезьяна.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:06.060
The monkey swings through trees and loves bananas.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:08.200
Обезьяна любит бананы.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:09.760
Try the full phrase now.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:11.640
Обезьяна любит бананы.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:14.260
Our next c-friend is Akula.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:15.120
Akula.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:16.340
This means shark.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:17.460
Repeat after me.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:18.200
Akula.

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:21.220
Imagine a cool swimmer moving fast through the water.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:22.980
Akula плавает быстро.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:24.680
Say that sentence once more.

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:26.500
Akula плавает быстро.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:28.120
Now meet птица.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:28.880
Птица.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:29.980
This means bird.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:31.100
Repeat after me.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:31.820
Птица.

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:34.400
A pretty bird sings it song in the trees.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.200
Птица поет песню.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:37.300
Practice the sentence.

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:39.040
Птица поет песню.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.300
On land we find sabaka.

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:42.280
Sabaka.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:43.440
This means dog.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:44.720
Repeat after me.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:45.700
Sabaka.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:48.280
Your dog comes back to you as a loyal pal.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.320
Моя sabaka дружит со мной.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:51.560
Try the sentence.

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:53.400
Моя sabaka дружит со мной.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.620
Another c-friend is Koshka.

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:56.400
Koshka.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:57.300
This means cat.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:58.340
Repeat after me.

00:01:58.620 --> 00:01:59.080
Koshka.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.680
The cat naps on the sofa after a long day.

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:03.260
Koshka spits na диване.

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:04.060
Say it again.

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:05.540
Koshka spits na диване.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.820
A big forest animal is midwet.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:08.480
Midwet.

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:09.460
This means bear.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:10.580
Repeat after me.

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:11.300
Midwet.

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:13.880
The bear enjoys sweet honey from the hive.

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:14.860
Midwet.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:15.400
Yes, meat.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:16.640
Practice the sentence.

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:17.560
Midwet.

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:18.100
Yes, meat.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:19.980
Finally we have рыба.

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:20.780
рыба.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:21.720
This means fish.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:22.920
Repeat after me.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:23.500
рыба.

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:25.980
The fish glides through the water with ease.

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:27.520
рыба плавает воде.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:28.600
Say the sentence.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.160
рыба плавает воде.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:32.380
One extra word ties them together.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:32.940
Друг.

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:34.200
This means friend.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:35.440
Repeat after me.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:35.920
Друг.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:38.500
Your pet can become a true animal friend.

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:40.300
Мой друг это sabaka.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:41.220
Try the sentence.

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:42.900
Мой друг это sabaka.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:44.800
Russian noun scare-regender.

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.840
And that changes how we describe them.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.220
Кит is masculine.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:51.260
So the matching word for big becomes balshoi.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:52.800
Кошка is feminine.

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:55.240
So the same idea becomes balshaia.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:57.540
A big whale is balshoi-kit.

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:59.920
A big cat is balshaia-kошка.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:02.120
The ending shifts to match the noun.

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:05.320
Balshoia works for neutral words like животное.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:08.900
This simple match lets you build correct descriptions right away.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:13.660
In Russian fairy tales, the giant whale often carries whole villages on its back.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:18.260
People long ago pictured the whale as a magical helper rising from the sea.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:21.000
That image still appears in stories today.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:24.100
Want to know a secret about one of today's words?

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:28.080
The Russian word кит, and the English scientific term citation,

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:31.120
both trace back to the same ancient Greek root.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:33.140
That root meant sea monster.

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:36.660
The word traveled through Latin into Russian as кит,

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:39.080
while English kept it mainly in science.

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:43.040
Watch out though, кит sounds a little like the English word кит,

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:45.920
yet it names a giant whale instead of a small toolbox.

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:49.960
Whenever you meet cetation in English, recall its cousin кит

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:51.620
from the Greek sea monster root.

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:54.420
That link gives you an instant memory shortcut.

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:56.420
Let's review with a quick challenge.

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:58.460
Do you remember what кит means?

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:00.160
What about akula?

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:04.320
Try saying the Russian name for your favorite animal three times out loud.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:07.980
For a fun activity, draw the animal and label it

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:09.660
with the Russian word you just learned.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:10.620
Молодец.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:12.100
That means well done.

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:15.140
Remember, every expert started as a beginner,

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:18.580
practicing today's words out loud, even just once,

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.760
and you'll be amazed how fast you learn.

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:22.040
See you next time.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:22.460
Пока.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:23.920
That's Russian for bye.

